# Welcome to MarkUP

This is a sample workspace. Everything here is stored in your browser, so feel free to edit,
rename and delete — **Reset samples** in the command palette brings the originals back.

::toc[In this file]{depth=2}

## Find your way around

| Action | Shortcut |
|:--|:--|
| Command palette | :kbd[Ctrl+Shift+P] |
| Quick open a file | :kbd[Ctrl+P] |
| Go to heading or component | :kbd[Ctrl+Shift+O] |
| Search in all files | :kbd[Ctrl+Shift+F] |
| Toggle editor / split / preview | :kbd[Ctrl+\\] |
| Save | :kbd[Ctrl+S] |
| Settings | :kbd[Ctrl+,] |

:::tip[Try it]
Type `:::` on an empty line to get a list of components, then press :kbd[Enter].
Inside `{…}` you get attribute suggestions, and inside a `chart` you get data keys.
:::

